 "podman": {
  "overview": "Podman is a daemonless container engine that runs OCI containers, with a Docker-compatible CLI, rootless operation and pods. It is for developers and administrators who want container workflows without a long-running root daemon.",
  "shots": [],
  "when": "- You want to run containers without a background daemon running as root.\n- You want rootless containers for a developer workstation or shared machine.\n- You want the same container commands as Docker for pulling, running, and inspecting images.\n- You need containers grouped into pods, which the docs describe as a Podman feature.",
  "how": "- Podman is a command-line utility built on the libpod library for creating and maintaining containers.\n- Typical flow: `podman pull` an image by its full name, `podman run -d -p` to start it with port forwarding, then `podman ps`, `podman logs`, and `podman inspect` to check it.\n- `podman stop` halts a container and `podman rm` removes it; `-l` refers to the latest container.\n- Rootless mode is supported; a rootless container gets no IP address, so port forwarding is the way to reach it.\n- Checkpointing can save a container's process state to disk for later restore or migration.",
  "notFor": "- Kubernetes cluster management; use kubectl, Helm, or k9s.\n- A GUI-first desktop experience; Docker Desktop or Podman Desktop-style tools fit that better.\n- Workflows that depend on a specific Docker daemon feature; check compatibility first. Not found on the official page.",
  "commands": [
   {
    "method": "Arch package",
    "command": "sudo pacman -S podman",
    "root": "yes",
    "source": ""
   },
   {
    "method": "Rootless helpers",
    "command": "sudo pacman -S passt fuse-overlayfs crun",
    "root": "yes",
    "source": ""
   }
  ],
  "commandsStatus": "Verified against an official source (install section above)."
 },
