  "when": "- You need free, open-source software for photo retouching, image composition, or image authoring.\n- You need pixel-level work such as cloning, healing, dodging and burning, or painting on bitmaps.\n- You need layer-based compositing with masks, layer groups, and blend modes.\n- You need to export images for the web in formats such as PNG, JPEG, WebP, GIF, or HEIF.",
  "how": "- The Toolbox holds the tools and their options; the Image Window shows the picture being edited.\n- Layers, Channels, Paths, Brushes, and Undo History are dialogs that dock or float beside the image.\n- Selections (rectangle, ellipse, lasso, fuzzy select, foreground select, scissors) limit where edits apply; they can be feathered or edited in Quick Mask.\n- Filters are grouped by effect (Blur, Distort, Noise, Artistic, and others) and apply to the selected layer.",
