  "how": "- A note holds information split into fields, such as a word and its translation.\n- Each note creates one card per card type; a card type is a question-and-answer template.\n- A note type defines the fields and card types, and is shared across the whole collection.\n- Decks group cards for separate study and can be nested with \"::\"; each deck has its own settings.\n- In a review session you see the question, click Show Answer, then rate how well you knew it, which sets when the card returns.",
  "notFor": "- Notes, planning or long-form writing; use a document editor.\n- Learning that needs hands-on practice rather than recall; use a course or tutorial app.",
